course: dictionary
lesson: 9073
title: Sliver: a thin, small piece
level: primary-6
stars: 2
explain: A sliver is a very thin, small piece that has been cut or broken off something. You can also use it for a tiny amount, as in «a sliver of hope». Read the words around it to find which meaning fits.
explain: «Looking at the Sun during an eclipse is not safe: even a sliver can burn the retina.» Here a sliver is a tiny part of the Sun's light, and it is still dangerous. The clue is the word «even»: a very small amount can still do harm.
explain: «When something breaks, the real danger is the broken pieces: tiny glass slivers fly far and cut bare feet.» A sliver of glass is a thin, sharp piece. The clues are «broken» and «cut», so you know it is a piece, not a tiny amount.
explain: Some words change with the place you live. In parts of the USA and Canada, a sliver can also be a splinter in your skin. Check the sentence first, and if it still does not make sense, use a dictionary.
fact: A sliver is a very thin, small piece cut or broken off something.
fact: A sliver can also mean a tiny amount, as in «a sliver of hope».
fact: «Sliver of moon» means only a thin, small part of the moon can be seen.
fact: The retina is the seeing layer at the back of the eye.
fact: In parts of the USA and Canada, a sliver is a splinter in your skin.
exercise: In «a sliver of cake», what does sliver mean? | A big, heavy box | A crumb of paper | A whole cake | *A thin, small piece
exercise: «A sliver of hope» means what? | Hope that has been lost | A huge amount of hope | *A tiny amount of hope
exercise: In parts of the USA and Canada, what can a sliver mean? | A type of bird | *A splinter in your skin | A loud noise | A big wave in the sea
test: «Even a sliver can burn the retina.» What is the retina? | *The seeing layer at the back of the eye | A bone in the leg | The top of the head | A kind of glass
test: «Tiny glass slivers fly far and cut bare feet.» What should you do when something breaks? | Pick up every piece with bare hands | *Stop, keep others away and tell a grown-up | Hide the pieces under the rug | Run through the room to find the rest
exam: In «a sliver of moon», what does the moon look like? | *Only a thin, small part can be seen | Hidden completely behind a cloud | Bright red | Full and round
